// Dialog :
"P1298811467" "Desperation, deprivation and despair are floating through the halls of Haven House now that everyone has heard about what you've done. I had a young mother bring her little children to me in tears. <br><br>'Oh, Mr. Phipps! My little Elsie and Sophia ate some of the food {VillainName} poisoned, and now they've gone blind! What will we do?' <br><br>Oh, I tell you, it took all the control I had to stop myself from laughing. But I put on my most sorrowful and sympathetic face for them, and took them all in. You've made this dreary charity case a simply delightful situation. <br><br>Now, whatever will I do with a desperate mother and her blind twin daughters? Hmmm..."
// RandomFameString :
"P208056581" "I haven't eaten in days. I wonder if Haven House has any food?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL8_GV_Phipps_Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SadLocket 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2700461855" "A locket with a note in it."
// DetailString :
"P664252019" "This heart-shaped locket contains two pictures and a note. The pictures show two teenagers, a boy who looks like a younger version of 'The Quest', and a girl. The note reads: <br><br>'I wish I'd been brave enough to escape with you. Now they're going to turn me into a monster. I'm so afraid, Jimmy. You've got to help me!<br> Trish' <br><br>Looks like her help is never going to show up now, thanks to you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P894943514" "People here at Haven House have something to be happy about, and that makes me angry. It seems that a young man who left the isles as a boy has come back, only now he's gotten himself super-powers. He's been working with Longbow agents, helping them get the lay of the land. He's also become a light of hope to the people here, showing them that they just might be able to improve their lot. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>That can't be allowed. I want him eliminated.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P2041013998" "Eliminate the returned home-town hero."
// SendOffString :
"P7601661" "The hero in question is called, if you can believe it, 'The Quest'. I've heard word that he's helping a Longbow squad set up a hidden base. Eliminate him, and that should do it. <br><br>Seriously, 'The Quest'! What kind of a name is that? I cannot comprehend the minds of these self-sacrificing fools who.. <br><br>Sorry, someone's coming. Have to get into character. <br><br>*Ahem* <br><br>You fiend, {VillainName}! You monster! Well, you won't win this time! Now that Jimmy Blenkenship has returned as The Quest, he'll put an end to your evil ways! This is the last time you'll be taunting me and hurting the poor people of the Rogue Isles!"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1999857819" "Defeat 'The Quest'"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P441199780" "'The Quest'! Try as I might, I cannot get over that name. Well, as long as you make him regret taking it up, all will be well."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P151357505" "Time to put 'The Quest' to rest."

